=== HIGHER TERMS ===
At n=19: α₄=5.52B, α₅=331M, α₆=4.1M
  α₆ counts 6-packings of 3-cycles (6*3=18 ≤ 19 vertices).
  α₆ is the only non-zero "imperfect" top-level packing at n=19.

=== PALEY VS CYCLIC ===
At p=7 (p≡3 mod 4): Paley H=189 > Cyclic H=175
At p=11 (p≡3 mod 4): Paley H=95,095 > Cyclic H=93,027
At p=19 (p≡3 mod 4): Cyclic H=1,184,212,824,763 > Paley H=1,172,695,746,915
WHY cyclic wins at n=19: Paley has more α₁, α₂ but cyclic wins through α₃+ by 26.7B.
Both n=17 (p≡1 mod 4, no Paley) and n=19 favor cyclic interval.
Crossover between n=11 and n=19 (no intervening Paley primes).

=== NEW ALGORITHM ===
The alpha_full_ssc.py implementation:
- Replaces naive O(|nc|^2) loop for α₃ (would take hours at n=19)
- Uses iterative SSC: G_k = cc ★ G_{k-1}, α_k = G_k[full] / k!
- O(k_max * n^2 * 2^n) total time
- 124× speedup for α₃ at n=17 (3s vs 372s)
